msgstr ""

#: views/settings.php:51
msgid ""
"The address that the phones use to register and to get their configs. A new "
"install has no value, and the configs do not work without it."
msgstr ""

#: views/settings.php:52
msgid "Internal server address"
msgstr ""

#: views/settings.php:54
msgid ""
"The address for phones on the internal network, when it is not the same as "
"the server address. Keep it blank to use the server address."
msgstr ""

#: views/settings.php:66
msgid ""
"How the phones get their config files: from the TFTP server, or from this "
"web server."
msgstr ""

#: views/settings.php:69
msgid ""
"The directory where the module writes the config files, for example /"
"tftpboot/. The TFTP server must serve this directory."
msgstr ""

#: views/settings.php:74
msgid ""
"The list is empty, so no phone can get its config. Add the networks of your "
"phones."
msgstr ""

#: views/settings.php:76
msgid "Provisioning allowlist"
msgstr ""

#: views/settings.php:77
msgid ""
"The addresses that can get a config over HTTP or HTTPS. Use addresses or "
"CIDR blocks, IPv4 or IPv6, with commas between them. The configs contain the "
"SIP passwords, and the phones do not log in, so this list is the only "
"control of who can read them. An empty list refuses all addresses. The list "
"does not apply to File provisioning."
msgstr ""

#: views/settings.php:79
msgid "Trusted reverse proxies"
msgstr ""

#: views/settings.php:80
msgid ""
"Keep it blank when the phones do not connect through a reverse proxy. Else, "
"use the addresses or CIDR blocks of the proxies. For a request from a proxy, "
"the module uses the phone address and the scheme from X-Forwarded-For and X-"
"Forwarded-Proto. The allowlist then applies to the phone, and HTTPS works "
"when the proxy ends TLS."
msgstr ""

